  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_scope",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1920,
        "y": 0
      },
      "text": "REAR WHEEL SPEED - one Y harness. RL and RR ABS drops run to the rear VRC in the back-seat area (rear driver-side frame); one screened 4-core output cable runs forward to the 6-way inline DT04-6P near the ECU (IX_WS_REAR). The ECU side owns only the short spur and the DT06-6S mating half (ST185-A-ECU). No bulkhead."
    },
    {
      "id": "n_vrc",
      "width": 390,
      "color": "Orange",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1920,
        "y": 210
      },
      "text": "VRC NOT DRAWN. The VR conditioner, its enclosure and its M8 panel connectors belong to the enclosure build, not this harness. Loose ends VRC_REAR_IN_L / IN_R / OUT are device endpoints: each lead lands on the matching M8 cable-plug pin when the box is built."
    },
    {
      "id": "n_shield",
      "width": 390,
      "color": "Orange",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1920,
        "y": 420
      },
      "text": "SHIELDS - VRC powered-device exception (docs/SHIELD-RULES.md 6.30). Each sensor screen floats at the sensor and lands on the IN endpoint screen lead (IN pin 3, wire inside the box to the case). The output cable screen is bonded to the VRC case and runs to inline pin 5, then on the spur to SHIELD_B (B17). One screen node, grounded once, at the ECU."
    },
    {
      "id": "n_iso",
      "width": 390,
      "color": "Red",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1920,
        "y": 630
      },
      "text": "TWO ISOLATION RULES. 1. The enclosure must not touch chassis - it is part of the screen, not a ground. Nylon mounting hardware. 2. The PCB must not touch the enclosure - nylon standoffs. The board grounds through the output cable only. If either is bonded, the screen picks up supply-ground noise and it will read as a flaky sensor."
    },
    {
      "id": "n_coat",
      "width": 390,
      "color": "Red",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1920,
        "y": 810
      },
      "text": "MASK THE THREE CONNECTOR LANDINGS AND THE CASE RING-TERMINAL SPOT BEFORE POWDER COAT. The OUT shielding plate and the input screen ring terminals need bare metal. A coated landing silently breaks the screen."
    }
  ],
